WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.990
At a cyber café, a student using the

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.890
free Wi-Fi on her phone asked me, “Can

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.130
the owner see my messages?”

4
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.130
Good question.

5
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.250
Let's find out who else can see what you

6
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.410
do online, and how to share less.

7
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.350
Today: Wi-Fi, trackers, and the data

8
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.110
trail you leave without noticing.

9
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.360
When you use a Wi-Fi network,

10
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.540
whoever runs it can see which

11
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.360
websites and apps you use, and when.

12
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.240
That could be the café owner, the

13
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.000
school, or a stranger who set up a

14
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.060
fake hotspot with a friendly name.

15
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.100
That's why the padlock matters.

16
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.610
With HTTPS, what you type and

17
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.730
read is scrambled on its way.

18
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.160
The network can still see which

19
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.200
site you visit, but not your

20
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.700
password or your messages.

21
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.240
And chat apps with end-to-end encryption

22
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.800
keep your messages unreadable to the café.

23
00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.570
Private browsing sounds like a cloak

24
00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.910
of invisibility, but it isn't.

25
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.150
It only stops this phone from

26
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.750
saving your history and cookies.

27
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.120
The Wi-Fi network, your school and

28
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.400
the websites can still see you.

29
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.020
Quick check!

30
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.060
Does private browsing hide what

31
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.800
you do from the café's Wi-Fi?

32
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.220
No.

33
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.730
It only keeps your history off

34
00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.150
this phone, which is useful on a

35
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.590
shared or family phone.

36
00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.190
Then there are trackers: small pieces

37
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.370
of code on websites and in apps.

38
00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.030
They follow you from site to site

39
00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.150
and build a profile of what you

40
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.850
like, to show you adverts.

41
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.960
That's why you look at trainers once and

42
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.900
see trainers everywhere for a week.

43
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.810
Many free apps are like a free bus

44
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.010
ride with someone on board writing

45
00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.630
down where everyone goes.

46
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.500
You don't pay with money.

47
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.300
You pay with information about yourself.

48
00:01:58.760 --> 00:01:59.620
You can share less.

49
00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.350
Make your accounts private, and

50
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.590
choose who can message you.

51
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.380
Turn off ad personalisation and

52
00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.120
location history in your settings.

53
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.190
And delete apps you no longer use,

54
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.130
because some keep collecting.

55
00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.010
Your turn.

56
00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.660
On the bus station's free Wi-Fi, which is

57
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.600
safer: reading the football news, or

58
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.700
signing in to pay with mobile money?

59
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.380
Reading the news, because signing in

60
00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.460
and paying can wait for mobile data

61
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.980
or a network you trust.

62
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.250
Remember: the network sees where you go,

63
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:38.030
the padlock hides what's inside, private

64
00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.010
browsing only protects this phone, and

65
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.790
trackers turn your clicks into adverts.

66
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.360
Try it tomorrow: open the privacy

67
00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.920
settings of one app you use every day.

68
00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.730
Turn off one thing you didn't know was on,

69
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.510
and tell a friend what you found.
